<title>SWEDEN: Volvo posts Q1 profit 5.25 bln SKR.</title>
<headline>Volvo posts Q1 profit 5.25 bln SKR.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish vehicle maker AB Volvo on Wednesday posted its results for the three months ending March 31, 1997.</p>
<p>					(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Pre-tax profit			    5,248 vs   1,924</p>
<p> Net sales				  41,849 vs  39,068</p>
<p> Cost of sales			    32,324 vs  29,979</p>
<p> R&amp;D					   2,062 vs   2,078</p>
<p> Selling costs			     3,681 vs   3,753</p>
<p> Admin costs				 1,686 vs   1,795</p>
<p> Other operating income		  1,028 vs   1,248</p>
<p> Other operating costs		   1,236 vs   1,535</p>
<p> Operating income			  1,888 vs   1,176</p>
<p> Assciated interests		     3,005 vs     239</p>
<p> Income from other investments	    57 vs     163</p>
<p> Interest income &amp; similar credits     993 vs   1,256</p>
<p> Interest expenses &amp; similar costs     803 vs     892</p>
<p> Other financial items	  CREDIT   108 vs	18 CHARGE</p>
<p> Tax					     717 vs     506</p>
<p> Minorities			   CHARGE  30 vs	11 CREDIT</p>
<p> Net profit				  4,501 vs   1,429</p>
<p>NOTE -- Volvo was expected to post a pre-tax profit of 5.10 billion crowns for the first three months of 1997, a Reuters poll of 14 analysts found. This was to include a capital gain from the sale of its stake in drinks company Pripps worth about three billion crowns.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
